# React Compiler

The React Compiler is on (`compiler: true` in `vite.config.ts`). Do not memoize by hand. Write plain functions and let the compiler cache values and callbacks.

- Do not use `useMemo`, `useCallback`, or `React.memo`.
- Do not use refs or effects only to keep a callback identity stable.
- Do not add `'use memo'`. The compiler already applies that.
- `'use no memo'` only if a specific function must opt out, and say why.

Leave generated `src/components/shadcn` primitives as upstream shipped them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const onSelect = useCallback((id: string) => {
    setSelected(id);
}, []);

const label = useMemo(() => items.find((item) => item.id === selected)?.name, [items, selected]);

return <List items={items} onSelect={onSelect} label={label} />;

// ✅ GOOD
const onSelect = (id: string) => {
    setSelected(id);
};
const label = items.find((item) => item.id === selected)?.name;

return <List items={items} onSelect={onSelect} label={label} />;
```
